language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ Choose a set of investments that stays within the budget and maximises the total net present value.
given budget : int(0..)
given cash_flow : matrix indexed by [int(1..4)] of int(0..)
given npv : matrix indexed by [int(1..4)] of int(0..)
find x : matrix indexed by [int(1..4)] of bool
find z : int(0..sum(npv))

maximising z

branching on [x]

such that
$ the sum of all chosen investments must not exceed the budget
(sum i : int(1..4) . toInt(x[i]) * cash_flow[i]) <= budget,
$ z is the total net present value of the chosen investments
z = (sum i : int(1..4) . toInt(x[i]) * npv[i])
